# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The editing tool (/admin). Copy to .env.local for development, and set
# the same variables in Vercel (Project → Settings → Environment Variables)
# for the live site. Full instructions: docs/TOGETHER-NOW-SETUP.md
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Who may sign in. One entry per person: Name:passcode, with :admin for
# people who can approve and publish. Commas between entries.
EDITOR_PASSCODES="Elijah:change-me-elijah:admin, Grace:change-me-grace"

# Any long random string. Signs the sign-in cookie. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=""

# A GitHub token that can read/write THIS repository's contents and pull
# requests, and nothing else. See the setup doc for how to create it.
GITHUB_TOKEN=""

# The repository the site deploys from.
GITHUB_REPO="gofaminttorontovp-church/GofamintTorontoWebsite"

# Optional: the branch Vercel deploys (defaults to main).
# GITHUB_BASE_BRANCH="main"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The photo gallery on the Media page, read from the church's Facebook
# album once an hour. Without these the page falls back to the
# photographs kept in content/site-content.json, so the site still works.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Facebook Page's numeric ID.
FACEBOOK_PAGE_ID=""

# A Page access token that may read the Page's photos. Made in Business
# Settings → Users → System Users: add the Page and the app as assets to a
# system user, then Generate New Token with pages_show_list and
# pages_read_engagement, expiration Never. Treat it as a password.
FACEBOOK_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN=""

# Nothing else is needed for preview links. The tool reads each change's real
# preview URL from GitHub, which requires "Deployments: Read-only" on the
# token above, and opens Vercel's preview login using
# VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET — which Vercel sets by itself once you turn
# on Protection Bypass for Automation. Do not set it by hand.
